      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nMake perf-eval build titles readable. Before: `(NIGHTLY=1) Evaluate vLLM 8cbd5d03... (CUDA)` ([example](https://buildkite.com/vllm/perf-eval/builds/658)). After: `[Nvidia] Nightly run 2026-10-09: commit 8cbd5d03...` (and `[AMD] ...` for ROCm).\n\n## Claims\n\n- Nightly perf-eval builds are titled `[<Nvidia|AMD>] Nightly run <YYYY-MM-DD>: commit <sha>`.\n- Manual runs (`RUN_PERF_EVAL=1`, `NIGHTLY` unset) are titled `... Manual run <date> ...`.\n- The triggered build's branch, env (`NIGHTLY`, `VLLM_COMMIT`, `VLLM_IMAGE_*`), `async`, and `soft_fail` are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Ran `.buildkite/scripts/trigger-perf-eval.sh cuda|rocm` with a stubbed `buildkite-agent` that prints the uploaded YAML. Output for `cuda` with `NIGHTLY=1`:\n  ```yaml\n  steps:\n    - trigger: \"perf-eval\"\n      label: \"perf-eval (Nvidia)\"\n      async: true\n      soft_fail: true\n      build:\n        branch: \"main\"\n        message: \"[Nvidia] Nightly run 2026-10-09: commit 8cbd5d03006c33185f402249ff2b448efd594986\"\n        env:\n          NIGHTLY: \"1\" # run all perf-eval workloads\n          VLLM_COMMIT: \"8cbd5d03006c33185f402249ff2b448efd594986\"\n          VLLM_IMAGE_CUDA: \"public.ecr.aws/q9t5s3a7/vllm-release-repo:8cbd5d03006c33185f402249ff2b448efd594986-x86_64\"\n  ```\n  `rocm` gives `[AMD] ...` with `VLLM_IMAGE_ROCM: ...-rocm`. Without `NIGHTLY`, the title is `Manual run`.\n- Both generated YAMLs and `release-pipeline.yaml` parse with PyYAML; `shellcheck` is clean.\n- Not yet run end to end on the release pipeline. The next nightly will show the new titles.\n\n## Details\n\nBuildkite pipeline-upload interpolation has no date variable and can't run commands, so a static `message:` can't include the date. The two `trigger:` steps are now small command steps on `small_cpu_queue_release` (same `key`, `if`, `depends_on`, `soft_fail`). Each one runs `.buildkite/scripts/trigger-perf-eval.sh`, which uploads the same trigger step with the computed title. Nothing else depends on the `trigger-perf-eval-*` keys. The date is in UTC, taken when the image build finishes. Tradeoff: each run now uses one short CPU job per platform.\n\nNot a duplicate: no open PR touches the perf-eval triggers. AI assistance (Claude Code) was used; the human submitter reviews and owns the change.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
